   "analytic": "costmodel.cycle_count, the basis every archived score was computed under: the stage and b combinations only, scaled linearly in state dimension",
   "traced_whole_step": "state_scaling.cycles_per_step from rk-work/trace/results.json: TRM-priced cycles for every instruction executed inside rk_step in one step, excluding the derivative routine's own body, measured at each of the four state counts the problem set uses"
  },
  "median_anchor_traced_cell_reading": "pendulum has the smallest median anchor error of the four held-out problems at 0.00412, so dividing by it amplifies any method whose pendulum error rises when steps are taken away. The champion's pendulum error goes from 0.00474 at 1,489 steps on the analytic basis to 0.026 at 455 steps on the traced one, which is most of why the median anchor ratio falls below one there. Read that cell as the metric magnifying one problem, not as the champion losing by that factor.",
  "note": "ratio = best classical held-out error over the champion's; above 1 the champion leads. traced_whole_step uses the compiled step's cycle count only as the budget denominator (how many steps fit in 65,536 cycles).",
  "source": {
